---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { toolIconSvg } from '../lib/tools';
import LongTailConverter from '../components/LongTailConverter.astro';

const title = 'Pounds to KG Converter — Pounds to Kilograms';
const description = 'Convert pounds to kilograms instantly. Free lbs to kg calculator — 1 pound = 0.453592 kg. Enter any weight to see the exact kilogram value.';
const canonicalPath = '/pounds-to-kg/';
const keywords = ['pounds to kg', 'lbs to kg', 'pounds to kilograms', 'lb to kg', 'weight converter'];

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'SoftwareApplication',
  name: 'Redd Tools Pounds to KG Converter',
  description,
  url: 'https://reddtools.com/pounds-to-kg/',
  applicationCategory: 'UtilitiesApplication',
  operatingSystem: 'Any',
  offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' },
};

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { name: 'Unit Converter', href: '/unit-converter/weight/' },
  { name: 'Pounds to KG' },
];

const relatedTools = [
  { name: 'Weight Converter', href: '/unit-converter/weight/', description: 'Convert between pounds, kg, grams, ounces, tonnes, stones and more.', icon: toolIconSvg['unit-converter'] },
  { name: 'KG to lbs Converter', href: '/kg-to-lbs/', description: 'Convert kilograms to pounds instantly.', icon: toolIconSvg['unit-converter'] },
  { name: 'Celsius to Fahrenheit', href: '/celsius-to-fahrenheit/', description: 'Convert °C to °F instantly.', icon: toolIconSvg['unit-converter'] },
];
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} activeTool="unit-converter" canonicalPath={canonicalPath} keywords={keywords} jsonLd={jsonLd} breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs} relatedTools={relatedTools}>
  <LongTailConverter
    mode="weight"
    fromUnit="Pound"
    toUnit="Kilogram"
    defaultValue={1}
    seoIntro={`The pounds to kilograms conversion is arguably the most searched weight conversion anywhere, and it shows up in everything from gym sessions and body weight to luggage allowances, parcel postage and shipping. The pound and the kilogram are the two everyday units people encounter most, and they belong to very different systems. The pound is the standard weight unit in the imperial and US customary systems used in the United States and, alongside the stone, in the UK, while the kilogram is the metric unit used for body weight, retail and science in almost every other country. Anyone who travels, trains or shops across these systems will need a reliable pounds-to-kg figure sooner rather than later, which is exactly what this free tool provides.

The history of the two units explains why they coexist. The pound descends from the Roman libra — the origin of its "lb" abbreviation — and was fixed once and for all in 1959 by the international yard and pound agreement, which defined one pound as exactly 0.45359237 kilograms. The kilogram, by contrast, was defined in 1799 as the mass of one litre of water at maximum density, was later represented by a platinum-iridium cylinder held in France, and was finally redefined in 2019 using Planck's constant. All of that history collapses into one constant figure you actually need: one pound equals 0.453592 kilograms.

The maths is straightforward. To convert pounds to kilograms, multiply the number of pounds by 0.453592; to work the other way, divide the kilograms by 0.453592 or multiply by 2.2046. For a handy reference table, remember that 1 lb = 0.454 kg, 5 lb = 2.27 kg, 10 lb = 4.54 kg, 50 lb = 22.68 kg, 100 lb = 45.36 kg, 150 lb = 68.04 kg, and 200 lb = 90.72 kg. Real-world anchors help you sanity-check any result: a 45 lb Olympic barbell plate is 20.41 kg, a 170 lb adult weighs about 77.1 kg, and a typical 50 lb bag of pet food is 22.68 kg.

Where does this conversion come up in daily life? Body weight is by far the most common case — bathroom scales in the US and UK display pounds, while medical records, passports, health apps and most other countries use kilograms, so anyone moving between systems needs to switch comfortably. Airline baggage allowances are another frequent trap: a common limit of 23 kg converts to 50.7 lb, while a 50 lb allowance converts back to 22.68 kg, and knowing which unit your airline quotes avoids surprise excess charges. Postage and courier services quote parcel weight differently by region, and gyms alternate between kilogram and pound plates depending on the equipment brand, so a reliable converter saves a great deal of arithmetic.

For mental maths, a reliable shortcut is to divide the pound figure by 2.2 to get a close estimate in kilograms — so 110 lb ≈ 50 kg and 220 lb ≈ 100 kg. This shortcut is accurate to within roughly a fifth of a per cent, which is plenty for everyday purposes. Whenever precision truly matters, whether for medical dosing, scientific work, competition weight classes, freight pricing or packaging regulations, use the exact factor of 0.453592 or simply enter the value in the converter below for an instant, exact answer every time.`}
    faqs={[
      { q: 'How many kilograms are in a pound?', a: 'One pound is exactly 0.453592 kilograms. To convert pounds to kg, multiply the number of pounds by 0.453592. To convert back, divide kg by 0.453592, or multiply the kilograms by 2.2046 to get pounds.' },
      { q: 'What is 150 pounds in kilograms?', a: '150 pounds is 68.04 kilograms. This is one of the most commonly asked body weight conversions, around a typical adult weight in many countries.' },
      { q: 'What is 200 pounds in kilograms?', a: '200 pounds is 90.72 kilograms. It is a common milestone weight in fitness and bodybuilding discussions, so it is a useful reference to remember.' },
      { q: 'How do I convert pounds to kg in my head?', a: 'Divide the pound value by 2.2 for a close mental estimate. So 110 lb divided by 2.2 is 50 kg (exact: 49.90 kg). For slightly better precision, divide by 2.205.' },
      { q: 'What is 100 pounds in kilograms?', a: '100 pounds is exactly 45.36 kg. This is a convenient figure because 100 lb and 45 kg are so close, making it an easy landmark for weighing things like luggage, produce or dogs.' },
      { q: 'Is a kilogram heavier than a pound?', a: 'Yes — a kilogram is about 2.2 times heavier than a pound. One kg equals 2.2046 lb, so a kilogram weight will always be a smaller number than the same weight in pounds.' },
      { q: 'What is 50 kg in pounds?', a: '50 kg is 110.23 pounds. This is a very common weight for gym dumbbells, kettlebells and barbell loads, and for the weight of an average European woman.' },
      { q: 'How many pounds in a stone?', a: 'A stone is 14 pounds, which is 6.35 kilograms. The stone is still used in the UK for body weight, so converting stone to kg means multiplying the stone by 6.35.' },
      { q: 'Why is a kg to lbs conversion so common?', a: 'Because the US, and to an extent the UK, measure body weight and many everyday items in pounds, while most other countries use kilograms. Anyone crossing these systems, or following US fitness content, needs the conversion.' },
      { q: 'How accurate is this pounds to kilograms converter?', a: 'The converter uses the exact factor of 0.453592 kg per pound, giving results precise to several decimal places — more than enough for body weight, gym, cooking, travel and shipping.' },
    ]}
  />
</Layout>
